{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-76","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：不可公度量与可公度量与中项无理线段","englishTitle":"If from a straight line there be subtracted a straight line which is incommensurable in square with the whole and which with the whole makes the squares on them added together rational, but the rectangle contained by them medial, the remainder is irrational; and let it be called minor.","book":10,"number":76,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.76","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_2.76/","group":"prop_2","sourceNumber":76,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-76@raw-321ff18fc492d051","contentId":"euclid-10-76","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"321ff18fc492d05156f162c9f71c7eaa51f0099d0ca3999e5ef511f8a9a1a00d","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-76.statement","euclid-10-76.proof.1","euclid-10-76.proof.2","euclid-10-76.proof.3","euclid-10-76.proof.4","euclid-10-76.proof.5","euclid-10-76.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-76.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-76","revisionId":"euclid-10-76@raw-321ff18fc492d051","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"54067ee76601759ff62e00e847d2366e333e404073a36b03af18f02ffc7caaeb","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If from a straight line there be subtracted a straight line which is incommensurable in square with the whole and which with the whole makes the squares on them added together rational, but the rectangle contained by them medial, the remainder is irrational; and let it be called minor."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果从一条直线中减去一条直线,即正方形的不可公度整条,而这条直线则使正方形直线加在一起有理,但由中项无理线段直线组成的矩形,其余的则无理,并称之为小线。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-76.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-76","revisionId":"euclid-10-76@raw-321ff18fc492d051","order":1,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"4700845e95b0a5d7d1043040385244d7e1d0294a1722903e6bf12aa71ad4b1b4","citations":["euclid-10-33"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For from the straight line AB let there be subtracted the straight line BC which is incommensurable in square with the whole and fulfils the given conditions. [[X. 33](/principles/euclid-10-33)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"从直线 AB中减去直线 BC,即正方形的不可公度整线,并满足了规定的条件。 [[X. 33](/principles/euclid-10-33)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-76.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-76","revisionId":"euclid-10-76@raw-321ff18fc492d051","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"709e94c10dfd6186bb9d319705c51b37bac20224fe1e270ccf3031a7ea8aeae6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"I say that the remainder AC is the irrational straight line called minor."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"我说剩下的AC是无理线段"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-76.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-10-76","revisionId":"euclid-10-76@raw-321ff18fc492d051","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d8353284d37eda6b8cd545cad920b6dbfeb426adef9190d635c9ae64c0cf9e47","citations":["euclid-2-7","euclid-10-16"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since the sum of the squares on AB, BC is rational, while twice the rectangle AB, BC is medial, therefore the squares on AB, BC are incommensurable with twice the rectangle AB, BC; and, convertendo, the squares on AB, BC are incommensurable with the remainder, the square on AC. [[II. 7](/principles/euclid-2-7), [X. 16](/principles/euclid-10-16)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为,由于AB的正方形和是有理,而矩形和AB的两倍是中项无理线段,BC是中项无理线段,因此,AB的正方形和不可公度是不可公度,而矩形和AB的两倍;以及,AB和BC的正方形和其余的不可公度,正方形和AC [ [II. 7](/principles/euclid-2-7) [X. 16](/principles/euclid-10-16)"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-76.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-10-76","revisionId":"euclid-10-76@raw-321ff18fc492d051","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d0257b4366073713f21d3c6fa9a1bc1427ca265aa1cac0ecf64412234a60ac86","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the squares on AB, BC are rational; therefore the square on AC is irrational; therefore AC is irrational."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但AB的正方形,BC的有理,AC的正方形是无理,AC的无理。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-76.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-10-76","revisionId":"euclid-10-76@raw-321ff18fc492d051","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"51de1097fc1e192a92acf3ce79d52e31dd0202b7e10e411c53e50415754473db","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And let it be called minor."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让它被称为未成年人"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-76.source","contentId":"euclid-10-76","revisionId":"euclid-10-76@raw-321ff18fc492d051","order":6,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ff4f8dc9461856982bb1850193fa112972ff381100bfd27fe434dddb129ce3d3","cit